+### Latest tech notes
+
+- Dropping PostgreSQL `CHECK (free_units >= 0)` is the correct way to allow Override-driven negative free; use `DROP CONSTRAINT IF EXISTS` (idempotent). Keep application-level `free > 0` guard on **non-Override** paths.
+- Do **not** use `GREATEST(free_units - 1, 0)` on Override consume ΓÇö that floors and violates FR-32.
+- Industry HRIS separates policy exemption (no seat consumed) from managerial override (explicit over-capacity) ΓÇö Divan mirrors this as Exemption (FR-29) vs Override (FR-32).
+- Reservation ledger already has `UNIQUE(event_id)` ΓÇö Start reserve must reuse it (one reservation per event).
